}


// NOTE (AI): The S00PacketKeepAlive branch is the capture half of Erisium mode: it stores the key and arms the replay timer. The replay half lives in the EventUpdate handler, which every 1500ms pushes C00PacketKeepAlive(lastKey) through sendPacketNoEvent, bypassing the event bus. Because the send-side branch cancels the real echo, the server's key comparison keeps failing and the ping EMA never updates, freezing the tab-list ping instead of letting it grow.

